AAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-226_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"f5243f27-ee4f-4752-bd07-9bbe31d60cab","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Source verification (2026-08-09): the ticket's original hypothesis that the intended source was rebar epic 3006-e198-13db-4e1f is DISPROVED. 3006 was created 2026-07-03 — a month after these citations arrived in this repository with the DSO extraction commit b534f47a7f (2026-06-08) and six weeks after the 2026-05-24 ACLI audit they describe — and its plan never mentions ACLI. The verified source is the pre-extraction DSO epic 3a03-b3f2-b34c-4e4f (closed, 24 children, 'level-triggered reconciler'), recorded in the DSO ticket-data mining report on the tickets branch under 63cc-ec94-4792-464b; it is the only DSO-era id beginning 3a03 anywhere in this repository's history, and the same file cites its sibling DSO bug ids (c916-74a1-ed06-40e4, 4fa9-0846-519e-4c30, 5010-1c6a-9387-4b5b) in full form. All three citations now spell the full id and label it pre-extraction DSO. Gerrit change 1572.","timestamp":1786309764096210001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit change 1572 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1572) merged to main 2026-08-09 with LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and zero unresolved comments. Commit 15432348c2 rewrites the three short 'epic 3a03' citations in tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_acli_field_coverage.py (docstring lines 10 and 13-14, comment banner line 415) to the full pre-extraction DSO id 3a03-b3f2-b34c-4e4f, each labelled 'pre-extraction DSO', so no reader is sent to the unrelated rebar bug 3a03-9863-542e-4ae1. Comment and docstring text only: 7 insertions, 5 deletions, no executable line changed. Verification: 36 tests pass in the module (unchanged count), make lint and make typecheck both clean in the worktree.","timestamp":1786313686802262001}],"created_at":1786118620601369001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"10accca3-0926-42b0-b9a2-b4add4facbdb","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c61a-9f8f-8ef9-4601"},{"link_uuid":"0e85b591-42c7-4844-b220-c01ef961a3b8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"612a-7fee-f2b5-402e"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_acli_field_coverage.py` cites \"epic 3a03\" in short,\nfour-hex form at lines 10, 13, and 414. In this repository `3a03` resolves to\n`3a03-9863-542e-4ae1`, an unrelated closed bug about the `_no_repo_root_leaks` test-isolation\nguard. A reader following the citation lands on the wrong ticket, so the provenance of the\nACLI contract-regression tests is effectively lost.\n\nThe verified source is the pre-extraction DSO epic `3a03-b3f2-b34c-4e4f` (closed, 24 children,\n\"level-triggered reconciler\"), recorded in the DSO ticket-data mining report stored on the\ntickets branch under `63cc-ec94-4792-464b`. Evidence for that attribution:\n\n- The citations arrived verbatim in `b534f47a7f` (\"Extract DSO ticket system + Jira reconciler\n  into standalone rebar\", 2026-06-08), so they name DSO ids, not rebar ids.\n- The same file and `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_graph.py` cite\n  sibling DSO bug ids in full form (`c916-74a1-ed06-40e4`, `4fa9-0846-519e-4c30`,\n  `5010-1c6a-9387-4b5b`); none of them resolve in the rebar store either.\n- `3a03-b3f2-b34c-4e4f` is the only DSO-era id beginning `3a03` recorded anywhere in this\n  repository's history, and it shares the prefix the author abbreviated.\n\nThe earlier hypothesis on this ticket that the source was rebar epic `3006-e198-13db-4e1f` is\ndisproved: `3006` was created 2026-07-03, a month after the citations landed in this\nrepository and six weeks after the 2026-05-24 ACLI audit they describe, and its plan never\nmentions ACLI. Citing it would substitute one wrong reference for another.\n\n## Approach\n\nRewrite the three short `epic 3a03` citations to the full DSO id `3a03-b3f2-b34c-4e4f`,\nlabelled as a pre-extraction DSO ticket so no reader mistakes it for the rebar ticket that now\nowns the `3a03` prefix. This matches the full-id convention the surrounding code already uses\nfor the sibling DSO bug ids, and it needs no new lookup table or doc. The edits are inside a\nmodule docstring and a comment banner only, so no test or assertion changes.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_acli_field_coverage.py` — lines 10, 13, and 414: replace\n  the short `epic 3a03` citation with `pre-extraction DSO epic 3a03-b3f2-b34c-4e4f`. No\n  executable line, fixture, assertion, or test name changes.\n\nNo other file changes. The sibling short form `bug c916` on line 409 is left alone: it does\nnot collide with any rebar ticket and its full id is already given on line 422.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `grep -n \"3a03\" tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_acli_field_coverage.py` returns three\n  lines, each containing the full id `3a03-b3f2-b34c-4e4f` and none containing a bare `3a03`\n  short-form citation.\n- [x] Each of the three corrected citations identifies the id as a pre-extraction DSO ticket,\n  verified by reading lines 10, 13, and 414.\n- [x] `git diff` for the change touches only comment and docstring lines in that one file,\n  verified by inspecting the diff.\n- [x] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_acli_field_coverage.py`\n  passes with the same collected test count as before the edit.\n- [x] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass in the worktree.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_acli_field_coverage.py","reason":"correct the three stale epic 3a03 historical citations without changing test behavior"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","612a-7fee-f2b5-402e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"ad984811-551b-4af2-8617-da3691277f5b","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["bridge","docs"],"ticket_id":"2380-e9b7-0d7c-4d0f","ticket_type":"task","title":"Correct surviving dangling 3a03 citations in ACLI bridge tests","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["95d0ca98-4bda-44e7-9758-0aa427418481","e33ec051-9c57-4408-b900-e52ab5d2a7ad","10accca3-0926-42b0-b9a2-b4add4facbdb","ca3b2ffb-6d4f-4709-88b1-8fbf12646195","c6294719-bfdd-49c8-a6c8-a9d41e7c502b","4e7dc874-a290-4641-bd64-92b502076c05","c9512183-b2a7-4f9e-a358-65bb77466ae9","287ff6ef-fe52-483e-8856-6d9bff283b64","0e85b591-42c7-4844-b220-c01ef961a3b8","a0c50f7e-4473-4b08-9c75-013ee4723867","ad984811-551b-4af2-8617-da3691277f5b","466155a2-dce5-45ec-908a-29c09ef55c2a","05ea48d9-06a2-43e2-a6dc-74648a3649b0"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659537771958001,"uuid":"53281338-8df9-41da-af12-6406dfa5a8d6"}